  "verification_note": "Full 16,384-unit actual-core equality passed in 329.62 seconds. All ten same-byte dual-checker cases passed in 174.545 seconds. Initial source cohort expectation {20} failed because ordinal original sources include both {19,20}; the test now pins the independently observed forms for each cohort. Previous basic/construction source cohorts and bytes remain unchanged. The first direct Any-fold test supplied a selector cube for depth zero, whose type is a Bool leaf. Its test input was corrected to V::Bit; no production term or checker changed. The initial Any-fold boundary test passed after its Bool input fix in 337.35 seconds. Fold counts were then changed to bounded bit splitting to remove per-node subtraction and arithmetic comparison. A subtraction-free intermediate run was superseded by the final bit-only branching version; its identified process was terminated intentionally, not counted as a test failure or checker rejection. The final bit-split implementation passed all five core test functions in 233.97 seconds, including the full-capacity case and all 405 Any-fold boundary cases. All ten final certificates passed same-byte dual checking in 64.555 seconds. Final source replay, fixture replay, inventory, lint and format passed."
